enchilada: GPU: arena BOs mapped write-combined into the client, no cache maintenance at SUBMIT/WAIT

25 s of opening and closing apps with 0310: SUBMIT still did ~3.2 GB/s of dc civac (~15 MB a submit,
~5 ms of CPU a frame), because 0310 cleans an arena BO at every SUBMIT once the client has mapped it
(clientMemoryForType), and Mesa maps its ~12 MB render target and many other BOs once and keeps them.
Linux msm maps GEM BOs write-combined (MSM_BO_WC) on a GPU that is not IO-coherent, so the CPU's
stores go to memory and nothing needs maintenance; this does the same.

- clientMemoryForType() names kIOMapWriteCombineCache for arena BOs. 0197's IOUserClient hunk makes
  a cache mode named there win over the caller's (mapClientMemory64), so this holds whatever the
  libdrm stand-in passes (it asks 0x401 = kIOMapAnywhere | kIOMapWriteCombineCache anyway). The
  withPhysicalAddress() descriptor maps through a contiguous device pager; memoryReferenceMap() sets
  the object's WIMG to VM_WIMG_WCOMB (MAP_MEM_WCOMB), vm_fault enters it with pmap_map_block_addr(...,
  object->wimg_bits) and the arm64 pmap makes that CACHE_ATTRINDX_WRITECOMB = MAIR 0x44, Normal
  Inner/Outer Non-cacheable. Device pager pages are fictitious, so the kernel's own aliases keep
  their attributes. Zero-copy IOSurfaces stay copyback with 0310's seed/age rules (unchanged).
- SUBMIT no longer cleans a BO because the client mapped it; WAIT_FENCE, CPU_PREP, CPU_FINI, BO_SYNC
  by pa, the first-mapping invalidate and GEM_CLOSE already skip arena BOs when boCached() is false
  (the CPU reads them uncached: fence words, query results and readbacks see memory directly).
- The kernel keeps a cacheable alias of the arena (the static aperture past the first 1 MiB window,
  0194). GEM_NEW now cleans+invalidates the BO once before the handle is given out (was: at its first
  SUBMIT, i.e. after the client's WC stores, which a dirty aperture line would have overwritten), and
  a command range is cleaned+invalidated before its relocations are stored through the aperture, so
  no stale line is merged and written back over the client's commands (after: as before, 0197).
- The 10 s line says how much of "left alone" was mapped by the client: "(0310; N MB of it
  write-combined, 0316)".

Boot-arg sweetgpuwc=0: copyback client mappings and 0310's maintenance, as before (sweetbocache=0/1
still overrides). sweetgpuflush=1 implies sweetgpuwc=0: copyback and everything at every SUBMIT,
wait, flip and lock. Costs: CPU reads of arena BOs through the mapping are uncached again (0197
measured ~50 MB/s), which only the fallback paths read in bulk (eagl glReadPixels with glzc=0,
glblit=0, glshow, traces).

